{"title":"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(cheap_method_using_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(cheap method using answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be39b3d4524a3a3ebd6afcdbbf78f21186dfa863.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x) = c_{2004}x^{2004} + c_{2003}x^{2003} + ... + c_1x + c_0\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coefficient\" title=\"Coefficient\">coefficients</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6ee7e962df3af21105dd1fa9af734da84f5a11e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{2004}\\not = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ae760d1ea10eb7a90d22087b3c7e2393d02117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> distinct complex <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zero\" title=\"Zero\">zeroes</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a9c0f8b68352372c3cb690d2728b2ada3ce739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k = a_k + b_ki$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b7266538fa53ab7a514de3b1cea423670509ea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq k\\leq 2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> real, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c65211d9ab6c9bd1af0f71a4194c6395c9791e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = b_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088ed1cd3d91f1acfc5dcedf987cb2799891cd91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{a_k} = \\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{b_k}.\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Which of the following quantities can be a non zero number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a903f18f1cc78cfc467b1a380e198def56cec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)} c_0 \\qquad \\text {(B)} c_{2003} \\qquad \\text {(C)} b_2b_3...b_{2004} \\qquad \\text {(D)} \\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{a_k} \\qquad \\text {(E)}\\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{c_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"486\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have to evaluate the answer choices and use process of elimination:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2f4283cfd441270cb90bfd2cf89a533f3dde81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />: We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c65211d9ab6c9bd1af0f71a4194c6395c9791e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = b_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78566a764f1fae77bd2d8419ce4697581f5115a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. If one of the roots is zero, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed77e1f41105bf2e59e41673c4dc500eb58cf58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(0) = c_0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5cf5dbc8229738cf06adbf2aa73fd75994b058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />: By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a>, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e633ad2a17f081c517b33c4f4a4a1b6864b81df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{c_{2003}}{c_{2004}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"51\" height=\"35\" /> is the sum of all of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Since that is real, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d822d7f62a3778d63ce32ea610ee7dd08d646379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{b_k}=0=\\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"149\" height=\"50\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68bc2d67753bc47cec47654b809eb962339ba0f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c_{2003}}{c_{2004}}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"72\" height=\"35\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e962de373f5c9a03e720b589cad1ec641478f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{2003}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2484f88154fadcf9c781bba19becdae88696b77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />: All of the coefficients are real. For sake of contradiction suppose none of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cdef8b7e5038334e5abfcc7689243fa6fc1b6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{2\\ldots 2004}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> are zero. Then for each complex root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">complex conjugate</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b1766ea42e0ae098ac7a98b6291fb41c425ca6b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{z_k} = a_k - b_k i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> is also a root. So the roots should pair up, but we have an odd number of imaginary roots! (Remember that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32f25f30e2bf419190d9774c0dd676b8d91f4b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.) This gives us the contradiction, and therefore the product is equal to zero.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbf4df7c25681bb178ddc50ee0c0d656aa25b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />: We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa92cb40ff17c0d81038a2b0623ba1d2df5049d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{a_k} = \\sum_{k = 1}^{2004}{b_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"116\" height=\"50\" />. Since the coefficients are real, it follows that if a root is complex, its conjugate is also a root; and the sum of the imaginary parts of complex conjugates is zero. Hence the RHS is zero.</li></ul>\n<p>There is, however, no reason to believe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea2b8f6b62721fc3e02ca622cd6da092a31bbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" /> should be zero (in fact, that quantity is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797a20647c81f3259c5069556cab51c94bf4b752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, and there is no evidence that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28cheap_method_using_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(cheap_method_using_answer_choices)\">Solution 2(cheap method using answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(cheap method using answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rule out answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff2a44a8501da3e1638aa408870d92b5a72f095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> as done in solution 1. Assume for the sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3faf1572d785ef1d5d72f120fb3a16190b4b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06cbe44ef79a2f21a5382b9bf4130b22dc5b9e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, so there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46225975937604afc8db1560a74c8328f59d76f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1f1499c468cb9119f97b83eec5e908f13da5c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_m=1+0i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, which implies at least one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16ab72a216b4eca45191b1e7ce387106054a50e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> SO if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bc93993324a1274865cc814226b591f056c140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{2004}c_k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"78\" height=\"50\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6950a790c9181c3bd3e5d51b4ccd33b51706da2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=2}^{2004}b_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"75\" height=\"50\" />. So we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f02391dbb8ec80d0d2515f62f9cfcd87b38dd74e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{2004}c_k\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"78\" height=\"50\" />, because then that would rule out all the answer choices. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea2b8f6b62721fc3e02ca622cd6da092a31bbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" /> must be nonzero, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3faf1572d785ef1d5d72f120fb3a16190b4b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.\n-vsamc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A\">2004 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017045142\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 328/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8462/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.143      1 -total\n 61.09%    8.029      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.28%    4.900      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5906:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017045142 and revision id 161636. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}